<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Acceptable Use Policy"
  description="What you may and may not do on avaTOK — across messaging, calls, live video, marketplace listings, consultations, and AI features."
  image="/og/acceptable-use.png"
  lead="The rules for everything you send, say, sell, or generate on avaTOK."
  updated="2026-08-05"
>
  <p>
    This Acceptable Use Policy applies to every part of avaTOK: one-to-one and group messaging,
    audio and video calls, live video, marketplace listings, live consultations, and our AI
    features. It sits alongside our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and
    <a href="/community-guidelines">Community Guidelines</a>. If you break these rules, we may
    limit, suspend, or terminate your access.
  </p>

  <p>
    Your agreement is with the avaTOK founding team — an unregistered business operating from
    Dehradun, Uttarakhand, India, currently testing an early product with invited users. See
    <a href="/terms#status">who we are</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who this applies to</h2>
  <p>
    Everyone who uses avaTOK — senders and receivers, buyers and sellers, consultants and clients,
    viewers and hosts. It applies to public content and to private communications, and it applies
    to what you do through our AI features as much as to what you type yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Prohibited content and conduct</h2>
  <p>Do not use avaTOK to do, share, host, sell, or promote any of the following.</p>

  <h3>Harm to people</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Harassment and bullying</strong> — targeting, demeaning, stalking, or repeatedly
      contacting someone who does not want to hear from you.</li>
    <li><strong>Hate</strong> — attacking or dehumanising people based on race, ethnicity, caste,
      religion, national origin, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any
      similar characteristic.</li>
    <li><strong>Threats and violence</strong> — threatening, inciting, glorifying, or coordinating
      violence, or threatening to expose someone's private information.</li>
    <li><strong>Self-harm</strong> — encouraging or instructing others in self-harm, suicide, or
      dangerous behaviour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Sexual content and exploitation</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Any sexual content involving a minor</strong> is absolutely prohibited, in any
      format, including AI-generated or drawn depictions. See our
      <a href="/child-safety">Child Safety Standards</a> for our full position and how to report.</li>
    <li><strong>Non-consensual intimate imagery</strong> — sharing, threatening to share, or
      soliciting intimate images of a person without their consent, including images created or
      altered to look like them.</li>
    <li><strong>Sexual services</strong> — offering, requesting, or arranging commercial sexual
      services through any avaTOK surface.</li>
    <li>Sexually explicit material in public surfaces, profiles, listings, or unsolicited
      messages.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Deception and abuse of the platform</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Spam</strong> — bulk, repetitive, or unsolicited messages, calls, invitations,
      listings, or engagement-inflating behaviour.</li>
    <li><strong>Scams and fraud</strong> — phishing, fake offers, advance-fee schemes, payment
      fraud, chargeback abuse, money laundering, or manipulating payouts, referrals, or promotions.</li>
    <li><strong>Impersonation</strong> — pretending to be another person, business, or
      organisation, or falsely claiming an affiliation, endorsement, or professional
      qualification.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform abuse</strong> — scraping, automated access we have not authorised,
      probing or bypassing security, reverse engineering, or interfering with the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Malware</strong> — distributing viruses, spyware, ransomware, or links intended to
      compromise a device or account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Illegal and infringing material</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Illegal goods or services, including drugs, weapons, stolen data, forged documents, and
      regulated items you are not licensed to sell.</li>
    <li>Gambling, financial products, or other regulated offerings where you do not hold the
      required licences.</li>
    <li><strong>Intellectual property infringement</strong> — posting or selling content you do not
      have the rights to. Rights holders can report infringement through our
      <a href="/dmca">DMCA / Copyright</a> process.</li>
    <li>Sharing another person's private information — address, phone number, identity documents,
      financial details — without their consent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Live calls, video, and consultations</h2>
  <p>
    Everything above applies during a live call or session, including exposing yourself, showing
    prohibited content on camera, or using a call to harass someone. If you record a call, our
    <a href="/recording">Recording &amp; Consent</a> policy applies. Consultations have additional
    rules in the <a href="/consultation-terms">Live Consultation Terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Using the AI features</h2>
  <p>
    avaTOK includes AI features, including the Ava assistant and an AI receptionist that can answer
    calls on your behalf. The rules above apply to anything you generate with them. In particular,
    do not:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Prompt AI features to produce content that would be prohibited if you posted it yourself —
      including abusive, hateful, sexual, or exploitative material.</li>
    <li>Attempt to circumvent, jailbreak, or disable safety measures, filters, or usage limits.</li>
    <li>Use AI output to impersonate a real person, clone someone's voice or likeness without their
      consent, or generate misleading content presented as real.</li>
    <li>Automate the AI features for bulk outreach, scripted calling, or resale as your own
      service.</li>
    <li>Use the AI receptionist to deceive callers about who or what they are speaking to where
      disclosure is required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    AI output can be wrong. You are responsible for what you send, publish, or act on, whether you
    wrote it or an AI feature did.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Accounts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account is for you. Do not share your login or let someone else use your account.</li>
    <li>Do not create multiple accounts to evade limits, suspensions, blocks, or promotions, or to
      inflate ratings and engagement.</li>
    <li>Do not buy, sell, rent, or transfer an account.</li>
    <li>Do not create an account if you are under the minimum age for your country, or if we have
      previously terminated your access.</li>
    <li>Legitimate separate accounts — for example a personal account and a business account, or
      accounts for different family members on a shared device — are fine, as long as you are not
      using them to evade enforcement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Enforcement</h2>
  <p>
    We review reports and may act on what we find. What we do depends on how serious the violation
    is, whether it is repeated, and the harm involved. We may take any of these steps, in any
    order, and we may skip straight to termination for severe violations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Warning</strong> — a notice explaining what broke the rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Content removal</strong> — taking down a post, listing, profile detail, or message
      we can access.</li>
    <li><strong>Feature limits</strong> — restricting calling, messaging strangers, selling,
      publishing, or AI usage for a period.</li>
    <li><strong>Suspension</strong> — temporarily disabling the account.</li>
    <li><strong>Permanent termination</strong> — closing the account and, where we can, preventing
      re-registration.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also withhold or reverse payouts connected to fraudulent activity, and we may report
    conduct to law enforcement or preserve and disclose information where required by law or valid
    legal process. Severe violations — child sexual exploitation, credible threats of violence,
    serious fraud — usually mean immediate permanent termination without a warning first.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      Enforcement is not a judgment about you as a person, and it is not always perfect. If we get
      it wrong, tell us — see the appeal section below.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>7. How to report a violation</h2>
  <p>
    You can report an account, a conversation, a listing, or a piece of content from inside the
    app, and you can block any account immediately, which stops their calls and messages reaching
    you. You can also email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. Tell us what
    happened, where, and when, and include screenshots or a link if you have one. We review reports
    we receive and act where a violation is confirmed.
  </p>
  <p>
    For child safety concerns, see <a href="/child-safety">Child Safety Standards</a>. For
    copyright, see <a href="/dmca">DMCA / Copyright</a>. Users in India can also use our
    <a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a> process. If someone is in immediate danger,
    contact your local emergency services first — avaTOK is not an emergency service.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How to appeal</h2>
  <p>
    If we limit, suspend, or terminate your account and you think we made a mistake, email
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a> from the address on the account.
    Include your handle and anything that helps explain the situation. We will look at the decision
    again and tell you the outcome. Users in India may escalate through
    <a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the product and the law change. We will post the updated version
    here and revise the date above.
  </p>

  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>.
    See also our <a href="/community-guidelines">Community Guidelines</a>,
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
